  "raw_text": "Step 1: Find a common denominator for the two fractions, which is \\(20\\).\n\nStep 2: Rewrite each fraction with the common denominator of \\(20\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{4+6a}{5} = \\frac{(4+6a) \\cdot 4}{5 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{16 + 24a}{20}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{1+3a}{4} = \\frac{(1+3a) \\cdot 5}{4 \\cdot 5} = \\frac{5 + 15a}{20}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Subtract the second fraction from the first:\n\\[\n\\frac{16 + 24a}{20} - \\frac{5 + 15a}{20} = \\frac{(16 + 24a) - (5 + 15a)}{20}\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Simplify the numerator:\n\\[\n(16 + 24a) - (5 + 15a) = 16 + 24a - 5 - 15a = 11 + 9a\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Write the simplified expression as a single fraction:\n\\[\n\\frac{11 + 9a}{20}\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{11 + 9a}{20}}<|im_end|>",
